---
import Section from "./Section.astro";
const faq = [
  ["Do I need the Akai MIDImix?", "No. Everything works with the mouse and the keyboard: knobs, faders, MUTE (⌥-click for solo), THROW, pages, gestures. The console adds the hands."],
  ["Other controllers?", "Only the MIDImix today. The mix logic never sees it directly: the MIDImix is a profile, plain data. A controller with the same shape (8 strips with 3 knobs, a fader and buttons, two bank buttons, a master fader), like the Novation Launch Control XL, needs only a profile. Pull requests welcome."],
  ["Intel Macs?", "The releases are built for Apple Silicon and nothing has been tested on Intel. Building from source may work; no promise."],
  ["Why does macOS complain at first launch?", "The app is signed ad hoc, not notarized: no Apple Developer account. Open Anyway once, or use the install script, which clears the quarantine flag."],
  ["Which stems can I load?", "Any audio files (WAV, AIFF, FLAC, MP3, M4A, CAF), any sample rate, any length; several stems can share a strip. Stems exported from a DAW, bought as multitracks, or split by the app itself."],
  ["How does it compare with a DAW or DJ software?", "Ableton Live, Logic Pro, Serato, rekordbox, Traktor, djay, VirtualDJ and Mixxx are great at producing or DJing. DubStemMix does one thing: a live dub mix of one tune's stems, ready on the MIDImix, for free. Each comparison is on the Compare page."],
  ["Is it free?", "Yes, free and open source under the MIT license. Bugs and ideas go in the GitHub issues."],
];
// FAQPage structured data, from the same list, so the page and the markup never drift.
const faqLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faq.map(([q, a]) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: a },
  })),
};
---
<script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqLd)} />
<Section id="faq" index="04" title="FAQ">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl divide-y divide-border border-y border-border">
    {faq.map(([q, a]) => (
      <details class="group py-4">
        <summary class="label flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm text-cream [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          {q}
          <span class="mono text-dim transition-transform group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-dim">{a}</p>
      </details>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-3xl text-sm text-dim">
    More answers, and fixes for common problems, in <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "")}/docs/settings/`} class="text-cream underline decoration-border underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-cream">Settings and help</a>.
    How it compares with Ableton Live, Serato, Amp FreQQ and others: <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "")}/compare/`} class="text-cream underline decoration-border underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-cream">Compare</a>.
  </p>
</Section>
